        "dependency_level": 1,
        "statement": "Let $M$ be a smooth oriented $3$-manifold, and put $R=\\mathbb Z[A^{\\pm1}]$ and $\\delta=-A^2-A^{-2}$. A **framed unoriented link in $M$** is a finite disjoint union of smoothly embedded annuli $S^1\\times[-1,1]$ in the interior of $M$, considered up to ambient isotopy through such framed annuli; the empty union is allowed. Let $\\mathcal L_{\\mathrm{fr}}(M)$ be the set of these isotopy classes and let $\\mathcal F_R(M)$ be the free $R$-module with basis $\\mathcal L_{\\mathrm{fr}}(M)$. For the local crossing relation, choose an orientation-preserving chart from a closed $3$-ball in $M$ to a standard ball in $\\mathbb R^3$, and project to the first two coordinates. In the displayed chart the over-strand runs from the southwest endpoint to the northeast endpoint, and the under-strand runs from the northwest endpoint to the southeast endpoint. The $A$-smoothing pairs the two top endpoints and the two bottom endpoints, and the $B$-smoothing pairs the two left endpoints and the two right endpoints. The smoothed strips carry blackboard framing. For each such local triple, the three framed links agree outside the chart. Let $\\mathcal R_A(M)$ be the submodule of $\\mathcal F_R(M)$ generated by $[L_\\times]-A[L_A]-A^{-1}[L_B]$ for all crossing triples, and by $[L\\sqcup O]-\\delta[L]$ for every framed link $L$, where $O$ is a zero-framed trivial circle bounding a disk in a ball disjoint from $L$. The **Kauffman bracket skein module** of $M$ is $$ \\mathcal K_A(M):=\\mathcal F_R(M)/\\mathcal R_A(M). $$ The relations are imposed on framed link classes; no unframed type-I identification is added.",
        "strategy": "Defines the free module and the submodule generated by the two local bracket relations using the KT-29 crossing convention.",
