        "dependency_level": 2,
        "statement": "Let $M$ be a smooth oriented $3$-manifold and let $L$ be a framed unoriented link in its interior with a specified component. A positive full framing twist is the local blackboard curl whose $A$-smoothing is the straight strip with one additional zero-framed trivial circle; a negative full framing twist is the curl whose $B$-smoothing is the straight strip with one additional zero-framed trivial circle. Write $L^+$ and $L^-$ for the links obtained by inserting these twists on one component. With $R=\\mathbb Z[A^{\\pm1}]$ and $\\delta=-A^2-A^{-2}$, the module classes satisfy $$ [L^+]=-A^3[L],\\qquad [L^-]=-A^{-3}[L]. $$",
