        "dependency_level": 2,
        "statement": "Let $M$ and $N$ be smooth oriented $3$-manifolds, and let $f:M\\to N$ be an orientation-preserving diffeomorphism. Then $[L]\\mapsto[f(L)]$ induces an $R$-module isomorphism $f_*:\\mathcal K_A(M)\\to\\mathcal K_A(N)$. These maps respect identity diffeomorphisms and composition. Let $\\Sigma$ be a compact oriented surface with a specified product collar $\\iota:\\Sigma\\times[0,1]\\hookrightarrow M$ whose lower face lies in $\\partial M$. The stacking product on $\\mathcal K_A(\\Sigma\\times[0,1])$ and collar gluing define a unital left action on $\\mathcal K_A(M)$: a closed framed link in the surface product is placed in a sufficiently thin outer subcollar and united with a framed link in the interior of $M$. The action is independent of the thin-collar width, associative, and natural under orientation-preserving diffeomorphisms that respect the specified collars. Only closed framed links are glued; no relative boundary endpoints are part of this action.",
