        "dependency_level": 2,
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice and let $R=\\mathbb Z[A^{\\pm1}]$ and $\\delta=-A^2-A^{-2}$. For a nonempty framed unoriented link $L$ in $S^3$, choose a regular planar diagram $D$ of its core. Let $m_j\\in\\mathbb Z$ be the full-twist correction on the $j$th component from the blackboard framing of $D$ to the specified framing of $L$, counting an A-type twist positively and its inverse negatively as in the framed diagram calculus, and put $m=\\sum_jm_j$. For a state $S$ of $D$, let $a(S)$ and $b(S)$ be its numbers of A- and B-smoothings and $|S|$ its number of resulting circles. The assignment $$ E(\\varnothing)=1,\\qquad E(L)=\\delta(-A^3)^m\\sum_{S}A^{a(S)-b(S)}\\delta^{|S|-1} $$ is independent of the diagram and twist corrections and extends $R$-linearly to a map $E:\\mathcal K_A(S^3)\\to R$ satisfying $E([\\varnothing])=1$.",
