        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and let $R=\\mathbb Z[A^{\\pm1}]$. Identify the solid torus with $\\mathcal A\\times[-1,1]$, where $\\mathcal A$ is a planar annulus. A simple closed curve is called essential if it does not bound a disk in $\\mathcal A$. Every framed link in this product admits a regular annular diagram and an integer framing correction from its blackboard framing. Let $z$ be one blackboard-framed annular core curve, and for $n\\geq1$ let $z^n$ denote $n$ parallel copies of that curve, with $z^0$ the empty link. In the polynomial ring $R[z]$, $z$ is also the formal variable sent to the core class $[z]$. Then the classes $[z^n]$, $n\\geq0$, form an $R$-basis of $\\mathcal K_A(\\mathcal A\\times[-1,1])$. Equivalently, the map $J:R[z]\\to\\mathcal K_A(\\mathcal A\\times[-1,1])$ sending $z^n$ to $[z^n]$ is an $R$-module isomorphism.",
