        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. An orientation-preserving diffeomorphism between smooth oriented $3$-manifolds transports the full framing of every link and induces an isomorphism of their Kauffman bracket skein modules. If the diffeomorphism carries a specified product collar of a compact oriented boundary surface productwise to another specified collar, the induced isomorphism intertwines the two closed-link collar actions. A positive or negative full framing twist on one link component multiplies its class by $-A^3$ or $-A^{-3}$, respectively. In $\\mathcal K_A(S^3)$, a positive twist of a zero-framed trivial circle changes its class from $\\delta[\\varnothing]$ to $-A^3\\delta[\\varnothing]$, with $\\delta[\\varnothing]\\ne -A^3\\delta[\\varnothing]$. In the solid-torus module, a positive twist of the blackboard-framed core changes $[z]$ to $-A^3[z]$, with $[z]\\ne -A^3[z]$.",
